        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b77776/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-27T04:58:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>How does line of sight work when the line between two hexes crosses \"blank\" space. &nbsp;&nbsp;<span>Is the blank space treated as elevation 0 (doesn't interfere with line of sight at all) or as elevation infinity (blocks all line of sight)</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For an example, consider Baron Blade Scenario 1. A line from the north end of tile 1 to the north end of tile 2 crosses an area with no map tiles. &nbsp;(assume north towards the top of the page, if you are looking at the map in the scenario guide)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:24.717Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 8,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 40.0,
        "yours": false,
